<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29256" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĭsĕrātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		miseror, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a pitying, pity, compassion, commiseration</i>
			(class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum quādam miseratione delectare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 5, 12, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miserationem commovere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 1, 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miseratione mens judicum permovenda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Or. 38, 131</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miserationem petere,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to pray for pity and forgiveness</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 8, 10, § 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infantis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just. 7,
					2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, rhetor., <i>a pathetic
				speech</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miserationibus uti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 21, 82</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicem inclinat miseratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 4, 1, 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6, 1, 23</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">4, 1, 27</span></i>; 4, 3,
			15 et saep.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
